FillVRegs' end case takes only the empty argument list (ADR-0033 a).

The NDK's clang (newer than Android 15's) orders the two FillVRegs templates differently: with explicit template
arguments, the end case, whose parameter pack is not deduced, is as specialized as the recursive case, and every
call of ArtMethod's Invoke* is ambiguous. A constraint keeps the end case to the empty pack it is meant for.

--- a/art/runtime/art_method-inl.h
+++ b/art/runtime/art_method-inl.h
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@
 }
 
 template <char... ArgType>
+  requires(sizeof...(ArgType) == 0)
 inline ALWAYS_INLINE void FillVRegs([[maybe_unused]] uint32_t* vregs,
                                     [[maybe_unused]] typename ShortyTraits<ArgType>::Type... args)
     REQUIRES_SHARED(Locks::mutator_lock_) {}
